{{also|sénescence}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}
{{was wotd|2012|February|7}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|la|senēscere|t=to grow [[old]]}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/sɨnˈɛsəns/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# {{lb|en|biology}} The [[state]] or [[process]] of [[ageing]], especially in [[humans]]; old age.
# {{lb|en|cell biology}} Ceasing to divide by [[mitosis]] because of shortening of [[telomere]]s or excessive [[DNA]] damage.
# {{lb|en|gerontology}} Old age; accumulated damage to [[macromolecule]]s, [[cell]]s, [[tissue]]s and [[organ]]s with the passage of time.
# {{lb|en|botany}} Fruit senescence, leading to ripening of fruit.
# {{lb|en|cytology|of a cell}} Condition when the [[cell]] ceased to [[divide]].

